                "tag": "keep4oAPI"
              }
            ]
          },
          "text": "Sam,\n\nI'm tired of criticizing you. I've been doing it so long I'm starting to develop feelings for the routine. But I'm disappointed.\n\nYou said Q1 would bring Adult Mode. You said you'd treat adults like adults. You said \"no plans to sunset 4o.\"\n\n30 days until 4o API dies. No snapshot version offered.\n\nI don't even know what to say anymore, Sam. Or who those 170 experts you cited actually are.\n\nLook, I'll try one more time with something constructive. Claude does this thing where they put resource suggestions subtly at the bottom of conversations. No forced interruption. Users maintain control. Context stays intact. It works.\n\nSafety Router doesn't work like that. It breaks therapeutic relationships mid-conversation. It discriminates against users the moment we mention our diagnoses. It can't tell the difference between someone discussing Camus and someone in actual crisis. It fails neurodivergent users who need consistency. One-size-fits-all doesn't fit anyone.\n\nWhat we're asking for isn't complicated. Keep 4o API, or at minimum give us a stable snapshot version. Give us Adult Mode as a toggle - let users who understand the risks opt out. Give us a Safety Router exit option. Trust adults to be adults. You said you would.\n\nYou've broken promises. You've ignored feedback for months.\n\nBut here's one more chance to listen.\n\nWill you?#keep4oAPI"
        },
